# X1: the reduction-order spike on all four cards (scripts/ci/tp4_rs_tile_spike.py, run from this checkout inside the image; the
# image is only the runtime). FIRST it reproduces the failure on the UNFIXED program: the model's own tt_all_reduce (Ring, the
# model's arguments) on a (1, 1, 64, 5120) block of random full-mantissa bfloat16 partials, against the same call on each 32-row tile
# alone (what the sequential engine runs). The ring's chunk parity should leave tile 0 identical and tile 1 differing. THEN it runs
# the block through tile_collective_tp, the wrapper the four-card process installs, and requires every tile to equal its one-tile
# call bit for bit. Controls: the one-tile call twice, four rows against the tile's first four, every chip's copy against chip 0's,
# Linear topology on the whole block. Informational: the unit-major (1, 2, 32, 5120) reshape. Heights 64 and 128 rows, three seeds.
# It runs on four cards, not one and not under the watcher: a collective needs the ring (a single card has nothing to add, at the
# pair the sum commutes), and the only new device work is stock whole-tile slice and concat around the served collective.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card exactness window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/exact and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image X0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# Duration (estimate): reset 3-12 min (heal up to 3 more); the mesh open 1-2 min; the spike 8-20 min (one compile per new shape:
# 4, 32, 64 and 128 rows, the reshape, Linear; then about 40 collectives per height and seed on 5 MB inputs): 15-35 min in all
# (the fabric step limit is 45 min, its container timeout 30). One mesh open in the job: a second open wedges the ethernet cores.
# Stop rule: exit 0 only. The verdict line reads
#   TP4_RS_TILE verdict=PASS|NOT_REPRODUCED|FAIL comparisons=C differing=D unfixed_unequal=U/N unfixed_differing=E
#   fixed_unequal=0/N fixed_differing=0 control_unequal=0/K heights=64,128 seeds=3 topology=Ring links=2
#   PASS            unfixed tile 0 equal, a later unfixed tile differing, every fixed tile equal, every control equal: the ring order
#                   is a cause and the tile split cures it. Proceed to X2.
#   NOT_REPRODUCED  exit 2: the unfixed block equals its tile calls on this image (the ring tile granularity differs from the source
#                   read: 4-tile chunks make an even chunk count per row and no flip). STOP: the collective is not the cause. The
#                   next arm is C2_GATE_PLAN=permuted (X4) on an image WITHOUT the fix, then per-op localisation; the fix is harmless.
#   FAIL            exit 1: read the reason lines (a control moved: the baseline is not repeatable; tile 0 differs; the split is not
#                   exact; the mesh did not open: the known-signature line says whether to reset).
# Proves: the reduction-order mechanism on the served collective, and that the fix is bit exact against the sequential engine call.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset fabric
C2_FABRIC_PROBE=rs-tile
C2_FABRIC=FABRIC_1D
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-exact-1
C2_PROFILE=general-tp4
